# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
# ── Derived caches (safe to delete; regenerated on demand) ──
#
# NOTE: cat_learning.db.clf.v*.pkl (the trained category-correction model) is
# deliberately NOT ignored. It is derived data, but Streamlit Cloud has an
# ephemeral filesystem: anything written at runtime is lost on restart, so
# without the model in the repo every cold boot there refits from scratch —
# minutes of CPU, repeated on every wake. Commit it together with
# cat_learning.db so the two match; the app checks and refits if they drift.

# On-disk validation caches
app_cache_flags/
app_cache_parquet/

# NOTE: app_cache_flags/, app_cache_parquet/ and cat_learning.db are ALREADY
# tracked (539 cache files, ~360MB .git). These patterns only stop new ones.
# To untrack the existing ones:
#   git rm -r --cached app_cache_flags app_cache_parquet

# ── Secrets ──
# API keys read by targeted_audit_filters._load_category_ai_keys().
# These were present and NOT ignored: a single `git add .` would have
# published them, and this repo is headed for GitHub / Streamlit Cloud.
keys.txt
**/keys.txt
.streamlit/secrets.toml

